<header><p class="st-kicker">colony · North America and Oceania</p><h1 class="st-title">Rupert's Land</h1><p class="st-meta">1670 CE – 1870 CE · capital York Factory</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The vast Hudson Bay watershed granted to the Hudson's Bay Company in 1670 and run as a fur-trading empire for 200 years before passing to Canada.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In 1670 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-ii-of-england">Charles II</a> chartered the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hudsons-bay-company">Hudson's Bay Company</a>, giving it trading rights and ownership of all lands draining into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hudson-bay">Hudson Bay</a>, named Rupert's Land after its first governor, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prince-rupert-of-the-rhine">Prince Rupert</a>. The grant covered much of what is now northern <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/province-of-quebec">Quebec</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ontario">Ontario</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manitoba">Manitoba</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saskatchewan">Saskatchewan</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alberta">Alberta</a> and parts of the northern <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-states">United States</a>, though the company knew little of the interior.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>For a century the company kept to coastal forts such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/york-factory">York Factory</a>, where <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cree">Cree</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assiniboine">Assiniboine</a> traders brought beaver pelts in exchange for guns, kettles and cloth. French raids under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pierre-le-moyne-diberville">Pierre Le Moyne d'Iberville</a> captured several posts until the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-utrecht">Treaty of Utrecht</a> in 1713. Competition from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-west-company">North West Company</a> pushed the company inland after 1774, ending in merger in 1821. Under governor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/george-simpson">George Simpson</a> it ruled the West, and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/red-river-colony">Red River Colony</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/metis">Métis</a> society grew.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/deed-of-surrender">Deed of Surrender</a> of 1869 the company sold Rupert's Land to the new <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/canada">Dominion of Canada</a> for 300,000 pounds, and the transfer in 1870 followed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-river-resistance">Red River Resistance</a> led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-riel">Louis Riel</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/ruperts-land.jpg" alt="Rupert's Land" width="320" height="160"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hudson%27s_Bay_Company_Flag.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1670 CE – 1870 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>colony</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>mercantile</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>York Factory</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Prince Rupert, George Simpson</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Indigenous religions, Anglicanism, Catholicism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Cree, English, French</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/canada">Canada</a>, <a href="/countries/united-states">United States</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Hudson's Bay Company territory, Prince Rupert's Land</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1770&amp;focus=ruperts-land" aria-label="Rupert's Land on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="2691 244 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Rupert's Land lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M3011 500L2772 698M3011 500L4970 663M3011 500L4997 651M3011 500L4997 651M3011 500L3203 831"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M2772 698h0M4970 663h0M4997 651h0M4997 651h0M3203 831h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M3011 500h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M3011 500h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1770&amp;focus=ruperts-land">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
